4. ARTIFICIAL INTELLIGENCE, MACHINE LEARNING, AND REVERSE ENGINEERING
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

4.1 No training or dataset use. You shall not use the Software, or any part,
    output, or description of it, to train, pre-train, fine-tune, distill,
    align, evaluate, benchmark, or otherwise improve any Automated System, and
    shall not include the Software in any dataset, corpus, embedding index,
    retrieval store, or vector database.

4.2 No AI-assisted reverse engineering or reproduction. You shall not use any
    Automated System to decompile, disassemble, deobfuscate, analyze, summarize
    for re-implementation, translate, port, "clean-room" re-implement, or
    otherwise reproduce the Software, its architecture, its algorithms, or its
    behavior. "Clean-room" re-implementation in which any participant (human
    or automated) has had access to the Software is a Derivative Work for the
    purposes of this License.

4.3 No human reverse engineering. You shall not decompile, disassemble, or
    reverse engineer the compiled Software, except and only to the extent that
    applicable law expressly permits such activity notwithstanding a
    contractual prohibition (for example, for interoperability under
    Article 6 of EU Directive 2009/24/EC). In that case, You must first request
    the necessary interface information from the Licensor in writing.

4.4 Obligations of Automated Systems and their operators. Any Automated System
    that reads, fetches, indexes, or receives the Software is bound by this
    License through the person or entity that operates or directs it. Such an
    Automated System must not reproduce more of the Software than is needed to
    help a user download, build, or run the unmodified Software, or to prepare
    a Contribution that the Licensor has approved in writing under Section 5.
    Operators are responsible for every act of their Automated Systems as if
    they had performed that act themselves.

4.5 Permitted Automated System uses. Notwithstanding Sections 4.1-4.4, the
    following are permitted: (a) search-engine indexing solely to display a
    link and a short snippet pointing to the official repository; (b) the
    Licensor's own use of any Automated System; and (c) use of an Automated
    System on behalf of the Licensor or an approved contributor to work on an
    approved Contribution.

4.6 Machine-readable reservation. For the purposes of Article 4(3) of EU
    Directive 2019/790 and any similar law, the Licensor expressly reserves
    all rights to text and data mining of the Software. This reservation
    applies to every file in the repository, whether or not it carries an
    individual notice.

